# chain (project_event_popup_arms) against a PLAIN owned county's keep tile
# — the gap sessions 14/16 left open (the only previously-known-clickable
# coordinate (260,250) resolves to an army, not a kind-1 county).
#
# Requires --save-ref pointing at a fixture built from the game dir's
# old_turn.sav/test.sav (map 17): those saves have exactly one kind==1
# territory record (k=4, col=30(mc), row=46(mr)) but it's owned by player 2,
# not local_player(1) — patched the owner byte to 1. Screen click reuses the
# EXISTING (260,250)/lParam 16384260 coordinate every other trace in this
# dir already uses (click_county.jsonl etc): that pixel resolves to screen-
# diamond cell (cell_col=4, cell_row=15) at ANY scroll, so patched the
# fixture's scroll to (col=20,row=62) — chosen by inverting engine_map_
# init_build_cells' rotation-0 diamond projection (sr=1+mr+mc, sc=(0x40-mr+
# mc)/2 => sr=77,sc=24 for (mc=30,mr=46); scroll = (sc-cell_col, sr-
# cell_row) = (20,62)) so that cell lands exactly on the target county.
#
# IMPORTANT gotcha hit while building this trace: the naive "TERR_REC col/
# row = scroll + screen cell" model (simple addition) is WRONG — g_tile_
# cells (the cursor's tile-index lookup) is indexed in ISOMETRIC DIAMOND
# space (build_cells' sr/sc2 sweep), not map (col,row) space directly, and
# the two only coincide for special cases. Naive addition landed on an
# unfilled diamond gap (non-integer inverse mc), silently resolving to
# county_id=0 every time despite engine_camera_cursor_to_cell reporting
# ready=1 — verified+fixed by reimplementing engine_camera_cursor_to_cell
# AND engine_map_init_build_cells' projection in Python and cross-checking
# against the already-known-working (260,250) click (which independently
# resolves to TERR_REC k=3, col=4 row=12 on the default reference save —
# matches the SCOUT dump exactly, confirming the corrected math).
#
